cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Awesome Self-Improving AI: papers, code and blogs on AI that improves its own model, harness and infrastructure"
message: >-
  If you find this repository useful for your research,
  please cite it using the metadata from this file (or via
  the "Cite this repository" button on the GitHub page).
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Hejian"
    family-names: "Sang"
    alias: "HJSang"
abstract: >-
  Awesome Self-Improving AI is a curated, continuously updated list of papers,
  open-source code, and technical blogs on AI systems that improve themselves,
  organised along three axes: the model (self-generated data, self-rewarding,
  self-play and zero-data RL, self-adapting weights), the harness (prompt and
  context evolution, memory, skills, workflow search, self-modifying harness
  code, evolving evaluators), and the infrastructure (GPU kernels, compilers
  and serving configuration, training and data pipelines, program and
  algorithm discovery), plus automated AI research, benchmarks, safety and
  limits, frameworks, and blogs. Each entry is annotated by what is modified,
  the improvement signal, and loop closure.
keywords:
  - "self-improving AI"
  - "recursive self-improvement"
  - "self-evolving agents"
  - "agent skills"
  - "agent memory"
  - "harness engineering"
  - "self-play"
  - "automated AI research"
  - "kernel generation"
  - "AlphaEvolve"
  - "awesome list"
repository-code: "https://github.com/HJSang/awesome-self-improving-ai"
url: "https://github.com/HJSang/awesome-self-improving-ai"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-09-04"
